A||||5||fiero56||Back from long trip||||10||
Z||000000||fiero56||12-08-2000||12:45 AM||||Just got back home about an hour ago(11:30pmET). Last week on Tuesday I left with dad in his Sebring headed from Dayton, OH to Roseburg, OR. Total trip mileage was 2,782 miles driveway to driveway. We took I-70 West from Dayton all the way to Denver(approx the halfway point), where we took I-25 North to I-80. Then took I-80 across Wyoming to Salt Lake City. SLC was where we took our <B>first</B> stop of the entire trip other than for gas. Dayton to SLC non-stop took just over 26 hours.  We left Dayton a 3pmET, arrived at SLC at 6pm(CT???). Spent a night in SLC then proceeded to take I-80 across Utah and Nevada, where we took I-95 North to I-104 West. We took another stop in Grants Pass Oregon. Well....finally arrived in Rosebug on Friday around noon. I drove past Brighton, CO(thought of Mike V.), and thought about the Batmobile driving near Kansas City along 70.<P>There is a lot of country I had never seen before, was definitely a very cool trip. Never saw antelope before, or elk, wild burroghs(spelled that wrong), tons of cattle, sage brush, or mountains. Pretty cool stuff out West. Can't wait to drive it again. Flew back home today. Left Eugene Oregon at 9am PT and arrived in Columbus at 9:15pm ET, with two lay overs in between. Country is a lot bigger than I ever imagined. A 12 hour trip to Ed's seems like an afternoon adventure right now. ||||reg||10
Z||000001||fierospeeder||12-08-2000||08:19 AM||||I cant wait to take a long distance trip, like route 66 with my fiero or motorcycle.  <BR>ive gone 7 hours in my car, illinois to northern michigan and back.  <P>Theres tons of places in illinois i havn't seen and its always fun seeing new things.  I always have the fear of something breaking down on me and i will be far away from home.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||12-08-2000||08:56 AM||||Long trips are neat in a Fiero. The wife and I do it all the time. The longest so far was Power Tour- RI to CA to FL back to RI- 81309 miles. Probably going to do it again this year Detroit to CA. To date 39727 miles in the last 16 months. Like the ads say "Drive Pontiac Excitement".<P>------------------<BR> <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/New-sig.jpg"> <BR>SC 3800||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||12-08-2000||09:17 AM||||56,<P>Good to hear that you are back.  Looks like Scott and Mike are online for Ed's in April.  I hope to deliver the 85 this weekend.  I don't know if it will work out that way though.  Give me a call, I will be outside working on her all day Saturday.  I did get that wire fixed :~)<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||14
Z||000004||Cheever2||12-08-2000||10:03 AM||||The West is the best.<BR>My parents took us to the west every year for a 2-week vacation, camping with the pop-up tent trailer.  The Rockies and Continental Divide were my favorite.  You gotta see Grand Canyon and Carlsbad Caverns too.  I never saw the Grand Tetons & Jackson Hole, gotta check that out sometime.<P>Editing to add that the cliff dwellings of Mesa Verde were pretty incredible too.<p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 12-08-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000005||87ECO5||12-08-2000||10:04 AM||||Welcome back, Drew.  We've got some catching up to do ...||||reg||1
